    "show_share": true,
    "description": "The Aga Khan University Institute for Educational Development (AKU-IED) recently hosted an engaging Kazim Bacchus Research Seminar (KBRS) session titled  What Should Educators Know About Darwin , led by Dr Kulsoom Ghias, Professor and Chair, Department of Biological and Biomedical Sciences, AKU. The thought-provoking discussion provided insights into Charles Darwin's life, scientific contributions, and the enduring relevance of evolutionary theory in education.",
